==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|keusaną|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|ǵews-||taste, choose|lang=ine-pro}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian ''kiāsa'', Old Saxon [[kiosan]] (Dutch [[kiezen]]), Old High German [[kiosan]], Old Norse {{term|kjósa|lang=non}}, Gothic {{term|𐌺𐌹𐌿𐍃𐌰𐌽|tr=kiusan}}.  The Indo-European root was also the source of Latin {{term|gustus||taste|lang=la}}, Albanian {{term|desha||chosen|lang=sq}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtʃeːosɑn/|[ˈtʃeːozɑn]|lang=ang}}

